  "body_html": "<h1>Von Neumann Morgenstern Axioms</h1>\n<p>For preferences over lotteries, the vNM axioms require the ordinary preference\naxioms together with lottery-specific compatibility conditions.</p>\n<p>The central lottery-specific axioms are:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>independence: mixing both sides with the same third lottery preserves\n  preference;</li>\n<li>continuity: if $L_1$ is weakly preferred to $L_2$ and $L_2$ is weakly preferred\n  to $L_3$, then $L_2$ is indifferent to a mixture of $L_1$ and $L_3$.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Together with completeness and transitivity, these axioms are the input for the\nexpected-utility representation theorem.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MSZ, Chapter 2, Axioms 2.12-2.17] Maschler, Solan, and Zamir, <em>Game Theory</em>, <code>references/GameTheory.pdf</code>. The vNM axioms for preferences over lotteries.</li>\n</ul>",
